{
  "info": {
    "title": "UAE Webhook Template",
    "description": "OpenAPI description provided **as a template** for guidance in implementing Webhooks under the UAE Open Finance Programme.",
    "version": "v2.2-rc2"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[subscription.Webhook.Url]"
    }
  ],
  "operations": {
    "/": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "UnsignedEventNotificationPayload_SignedEventNotificationPayload",
        "parameters": [],
        "description": "This endpoint provides a template for the implementation of Webhooks at a TPP.\n\nA 202 or 204 HTTP return code with an empty payload is expected in acknowledgement of receipt.\n\nTPPs should observe the standardized error payloads as defined by the Open Finance Framework and provided in this API\ndescription.",
        "summary": "Event Notification Template",
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Accepted",
            "headers": {
              "x-fapi-interaction-id": {
                "required": false,
                "description": "An RFC4122 UID used as a correlation ID.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "204": {
            "description": "No content",
            "headers": {
              "x-fapi-interaction-id": {
                "required": false,
                "description": "An RFC4122 UID used as a correlation ID.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/400Error"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/401Error"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/403Error"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/404Error"
          },
          "405": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/405Error"
          },
          "406": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/406Error"
          },
          "415": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/415Error"
          },
          "429": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/429Error"
          },
          "500": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/500Error"
          }
        },
        "tags": [
          "Webhook Template"
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEWebhookEventSigned"
              }
            },
            "application/jwt": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The Event Notification as it arrives on the wire: a JWE, in JWE Compact Serialization (five base64url-encoded parts separated by dots), whose plaintext is a JWS carrying the JSON payload."
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "**The Content Type is `application/jwt`, but the event is a JWE.**\n\n`application/jwe` is not a registered media type, so the Content Type header carries the registered `application/jwt` value (RFC 7519) for every Event Notification delivered to a Webhook. That value describes the container, not the encryption: the event is a *nested* JWT — a JWS, signed by the sender, encrypted inside a JWE addressed to the recipient — and it is the JWE that is transmitted. Do not infer from the `application/jwt` Content Type that the payload can be parsed as a bare signed JWT; it cannot, because it is encrypted.\n\nA recipient must therefore, in order:\n\n1. read the request body as a string — it is a JWE in Compact Serialization, five dot-separated parts, not the three of a bare JWS;\n2. decrypt the JWE to recover the enclosed JWS;\n3. verify the JWS signature;\n4. parse the resulting JSON payload, which is the Event Notification.\n\nThe `application/json` Content Type above is never sent on the wire. It is present only so that the Schema Object can document the shape of the payload recovered at step 4, so TPPs can see the message definition they must parse.\n\nPlease refer to the Open Finance Framework documentation for guidelines on decrypting and verifying the JWTs received at Webhooks."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

